From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] rtl8723bs: protect the TX free page accounting with the
 lock the driver already has

The driver keeps a software mirror of the firmware's free TX page counter
in hal_com_data.SdioTxFIFOFreePage[], together with a spinlock
(SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock) that the vendor wrote for exactly this purpose --
but then commented the lock out and left the counter unprotected.

Two writers touch the counter:

  * hal/hal_sdio.c:rtw_hal_sdio_update_tx_freepage() subtracts the pages
    it is about to hand to the firmware.  That is a read-modify-write of
    one byte.
  * hal/sdio_ops.c:HalQueryTxBufferStatus8723BSdio() overwrites the whole
    four byte array with the value read back from the hardware
    (SDIO_REG_FREE_TXPG).

If the two interleave, the read-modify-write can compute its result from
a stale value and write it back after the four byte overwrite: the driver
then believes in TX pages that the firmware has already given away.  The
consequence is the same failure this whole series is about -- the TX path
runs out of pages and stops.

Restore the lock the driver already had around the accounting and extend
it to the hardware query, so that the two writers cannot interleave.  The
SDIO command itself stays outside the lock, because sdio_local_cmd53_read4byte()
may sleep and a spinlock may not be held across a sleeping call.

Call sites and their context were checked: the two callers of
HalQueryTxBufferStatus8723BSdio() (hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c, TX worker, and
hal/sdio_halinit.c, driver init) and the callers of the two accounting
helpers run in process context, so spin_lock_bh() is the right primitive
and no lock is taken recursively.

This is the last of the hardware level races in the TX page accounting
that this series does not cover (see the README for the two known
defects that remain).

---
 drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/hal_sdio.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/sdio_ops.c | 10 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/hal_sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/hal_sdio.c
@@ -23,8 +23,14 @@
 )
 {
 	struct hal_com_data	*pHalData = GET_HAL_DATA(padapter);
+	u8 have;
 
-	if ((pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PageIdx]+pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PUBLIC_QUEUE_IDX]) >= (RequiredPageNum))
+	spin_lock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
+	have = (u8)(pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PageIdx]
+		+ pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PUBLIC_QUEUE_IDX]);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
+
+	if (have >= RequiredPageNum)
 		return true;
 	else
 		return false;
@@ -39,7 +45,7 @@
 	u8 RequiredPublicFreePgNum = 0;
 	/* _irqL irql; */
 
-	/* spin_lock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock); */
+	spin_lock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
 
 	DedicatedPgNum = pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PageIdx];
 	if (RequiredPageNum <= DedicatedPgNum) {
@@ -50,7 +56,7 @@
 		pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePage[PUBLIC_QUEUE_IDX] -= RequiredPublicFreePgNum;
 	}
 
-	/* spin_unlock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock); */
+	spin_unlock_bh(&pHalData->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
 }
 
 void rtw_hal_set_sdio_tx_max_length(
--- a/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/sdio_ops.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/sdio_ops.c
@@ -992,7 +992,15 @@
 
 	numof_free_page = sdio_local_cmd53_read4byte(adapter, SDIO_REG_FREE_TXPG);
 
+	/* The SDIO command above must not run under the lock (it may sleep),
+	 * so only the counter update itself is protected.  Without this the
+	 * four-byte overwrite can interleave with the read-modify-write in
+	 * rtw_hal_sdio_update_tx_freepage() and leave the driver believing in
+	 * free pages that the firmware has already handed out.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_bh(&hal->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
 	memcpy(hal->SdioTxFIFOFreePage, &numof_free_page, 4);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&hal->SdioTxFIFOFreePageLock);
 
 	return true;
 }
